One of their most memorable collaborations was *On the Beach*. Young and Burden worked together to create a surreal beach scene featuring a Cadillac fender, a yellow beach chair, and Young standing in the background.

The photograph captured the strange, disillusioned atmosphere of the album itself. Young later recalled the experience with great affection, describing it as one of his favorite album covers.

Their creative process was highly collaborative. Burden listened carefully to Young’s music before developing his ideas, while Young contributed his own concepts and challenged Burden to think beyond conventional design.

